OL,3,GNEWSALine in the sand: Council to ban
OL,4,Anew beach food vans
OL,5,
OL,6,FAberdeen City Council is to stop new
OL,7,Ffood and drink vans setting up at the
OL,8,Fcity's beachfront after concerns about
OL,9,Fthe number of street traders operating
OL,10,Fin the area.
OL,12,FA total of 36 businesses have
OL,13,Fpermission to set up there, ranging
OL,14,Ffrom burger and burrito bars to sweet
OL,15,Ftreats.
OL,17,FThe local authority agreed proposals
OL,18,Fthat will see no new licences granted
OL,19,Fwhile beach masterplan works are
OL,20,Fongoing and a temporary presumption
OL,21,Fagainst street trading will brought in.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,428,420,260,160,0,100
